WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
OK.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:06.259
It's I guess it's as good a time as ever to
have this conversation, if not now, when.

00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:07.259
Right.

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:09.960
And I know that there's people in my audience
who aren't going to like this.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.210
And they're going to be mad at me and they're
going to disagree and they're going to dislike

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.930
the video and they're going to unsubscribe.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:21.640
And a few, even the really special ones will
even say anti-Semitic things.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:26.810
And we'll say, I'm a bad person and I'm a
shill, but I can't care about that anymore.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.780
You know, I do stories as I see them.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.529
You guys have seen this throughout the election
cycle.

00:00:31.529 --> 00:00:33.490
Sometimes we lose 500 subscribers.

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.260
Sometimes we gain 500.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.260
Who knows?

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.260
I don't care.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.260
It's too serious.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.970
And so we have to do it.

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:42.480
Vote blue no matter who.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.980
Here we go now is not the same as vote Biden
over Trump.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.320
All right, let's think this through.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.190
We've got to understand this before things
swirl out of control.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:01:00.040
There is a very reasonable debate to be had
about Joe Biden's policies when Joe Biden

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:04.180
says he supports the Green New Deal as a framework.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:10.180
What does that mean versus saying he would
push for specifically the Green New Deal?

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.180
That's a debate.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.070
That's a great debate to have.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:18.740
But we can't equate vote blue no matter who
to saying.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:22.460
I believe Biden would be better than Trump
specifically.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:25.550
And there are many supporters who have been
correctly tweeting me.

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:27.120
I want to be very clear.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.120
You guys are right.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:33.909
When you say, David, vote blue, no matter
who relinquishes agency.

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:38.780
It says to the DNC, you don't have to earn
my vote because I'm voting blue no matter

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.020
who I'm going to vote for.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:46.340
Whoever has a D next to their name, no matter
who they are or what their platform is.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.450
That's absolutely correct.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:53.770
That being said, that's not what I or many
others are advocating for.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:56.920
I have never said vote blue no matter who.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.670
And in fact, I've said quite the opposite.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:05.909
All along I've said I evaluate candidates
and decide who's better.

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:07.660
It's not a party analysis.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:13.760
And then I say, do I prefer this person to
Donald Trump or do I prefer Donald Trump vote

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:14.760
blue?

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.209
No matter who would be saying, I'm not evaluating
candidates.

00:02:18.209 --> 00:02:22.510
I'm merely going to vote based on whether
someone is a Democrat.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:24.030
That's not what I do.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:28.170
Biden is better than Trump on a number of
different issues.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.500
I've talked about a lot of them.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.720
And of course, all of these are up for debate
on judges, including the Supreme Court.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.140
I don't want Trump choosing Ruth Bader Ginsburg's
replacement.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:43.200
I want Biden choosing Ruth Bader Ginsburg
replacement, if you would prefer it be Bernie.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.200
Great.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.200
That's not the choice.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.200
The choice is Biden or Trump.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.030
And I prefer Biden on climate.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:52.300
Biden supports the Green New Deal as a framework.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:53.300
Trump doesn't.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:56.270
Trump thinks climate change is a hoax created
by the Chinese.

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:57.750
Biden's better on that.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:58.750
Taxes.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.870
Is Biden's tax plan as progressive as Bernie's?

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:02.870
No.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.650
Is Biden's tax plan better than Trump's?

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.650
Yes.

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:08.190
On health care is Biden's tax plan.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:09.530
The progressive gold standard?

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.370
No, not even close.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:15.430
Is it way better than what Trump tried to
do a couple of years ago?

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:18.050
Of course it is on diplomacy.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.810
Is Biden an embarrassment?

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:21.800
Around the world the way Trump is?

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.800
No.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:28.489
You might not like the things Biden will do
with his diplomatic skills and with his experience.

00:03:28.489 --> 00:03:30.739
But there's no question that it's better than
Trump.

00:03:30.739 --> 00:03:38.150
So back when it was Bernie and Warren and
Amy and Pete and Biden, at that point when

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:41.520
there were five possible candidates who could
who could win.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.680
It still wasn't vote blue, no matter who it
was.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:50.190
When I look at these five, any of these five
individuals would be better than Donald Trump

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.430
and I would vote for any of them.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:58.660
When it was down to Bernie and Biden as the
last two contenders, I still wasn't vote blue

00:03:58.660 --> 00:03:59.660
no matter who.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:00.670
I'm not even a Democrat.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:06.640
Remember, it was either of these two specific
people Bernie or Biden would be better than

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:07.640
Trump.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:11.110
And likewise, at this point, this is not vote
blue no matter who.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:15.590
For me, it's given the choices we now have
either.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:19.400
Donald Trump will be reelected in November
or Joe Biden will be elected.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.570
And Donald Trump will be removed.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:26.300
That is the choice I am making and why I will
be voting for Joe Biden.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:31.210
And, you know, if the language continues to
be arguing about the principle of vote blue

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.610
no matter who.

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:34.990
We're missing the forest for the trees.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:40.080
The debate over vote blue, no matter who is
a principal, is a valid debate.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:45.319
And that's not the debate that we are having
right now in terms of whether to choose Biden

00:04:45.319 --> 00:04:48.779
specifically over Donald Trump.

00:04:48.779 --> 00:04:55.270
Now, you might prefer Trump to Biden by all
means than vote for Trump or stay home or

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.190
write someone in or whatever.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:02.069
But let's not live in this fantasy world where
we're pretending that this is about the principle

00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:06.889
of if the DNC doesn't earn my vote, then they
don't deserve it.

00:05:06.889 --> 00:05:12.080
Well, has Trump earned what is de facto your
support if you choose to stay home or write

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.110
someone in?

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:19.389
Because the idea that it's neutral to vote
for neither of them is one of the false notions

00:05:19.389 --> 00:05:22.740
that we've been trying to dispel for years
on the program.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:28.539
So if you're okay with your actions helping
Trump get get reelected, then do whatever

00:05:28.539 --> 00:05:29.539
you want.

00:05:29.539 --> 00:05:30.539
I'm not going to fight with people.

00:05:30.539 --> 00:05:31.539
I'm not going to attack people.

00:05:31.539 --> 00:05:38.180
I understand that there are many people who,
if it's not going to be Bernie, would rather

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:41.150
it be Trump than Biden either, because they
think that it's.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:46.410
A message to the DNC or they have a burn it
all down to build it back up mentality or

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.440
they want to punish you.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:49.440
That's fine.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:50.440
That's fine.

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:52.939
But let's just be honest that that's what
you're doing.

00:05:52.939 --> 00:05:57.460
If that is what you were going to do, I won't
argue with you on principle as long as you're

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:01.560
honest and take responsibility for what it
is that you're doing.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.580
I just don't want people to mistake.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:12.120
Vote blue no matter who wins, saying the options
are Biden and Trump and I prefer Biden to

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.120
Trump.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.240
Switch their party affiliations.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:17.699
Tell me Biden's the Republican and trumps
the Democrat.

00:06:17.699 --> 00:06:18.870
Biden's still better.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.259
That's the reality.

00:06:20.259 --> 00:06:27.020
Let's not mistake a debate over Trump versus
Biden with the debate over the idea of vote

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.020
blue no matter who.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:07:09.110
Cause that's not going to get us

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:42.639
very far.

